<description>
Expand each isolated marker into the edge legend string containing its color, aligned so the marker keeps that legend position.

Input structure
- The background is the dominant color.
- One or more top- or bottom-edge horizontal foreground runs are legend strings.
- All other foreground components are single-pixel markers whose colors appear in exactly one legend position.

Rule
- For each marker, find the unique legend string containing the marker color.
- Copy that string horizontally on the marker row, shifted so the matching legend entry lands on the marker pixel.
- Clip the copied string at the left or right grid boundary when needed.

Key insight
- The isolated pixel is not just recolored; its color gives both the legend string to copy and the anchor index inside that string.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "top- or bottom-edge horizontal legend string s",
  "dst": "isolated marker pixel d and its row",
  "match_cond": "d.color occurs in exactly one position of s",
  "transform": "copy the full s horizontally onto d.row with the matched color aligned over d; clip at the grid boundary"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12-17 rows x 13-18 cols, bg=0
  legends:
    count: 1-3 contiguous horizontal color runs on top/bottom edge rows
    length: 3-6 distinct non-bg colors per legend
    placement: each on row 0 or row H-1; multiple legends on same edge separated by >=7 bg cells
    colors: all unique within each legend; legends MAY share colors across legends
    total_legend_colors: 6-12 across all legends = all non-bg colors in grid
  markers:
    count: 3-6 isolated single-pixel foreground cells on interior rows (not on legend edge rows)
    color: each marker color appears in exactly one legend at exactly one position
    rows: each marker on a distinct row, or at most 2 markers share a row if from different legends [observed]
    no_overlap: when expanded, legend copies on same row must not collide
    clipping: 0-1 markers may expand beyond grid boundary (clipped) [observed]
  output:
    edge rows preserved unchanged
    each marker replaced by its full legend string, horizontally aligned so marker pixel = matched position
    clipped at grid left/right boundary

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid H x W (12-17 x 13-18). Pick bg=0.
    2. Design 1-3 legend sequences of length 3-6 using distinct non-bg colors. Ensure no color repeats within a legend.
    3. Place legends on top/bottom edge rows with >=7 bg gap between legends on same edge.
    4. Select 3-6 marker colors, each appearing in exactly one legend at one position (exclude colors shared between legends).
    5. For each marker, pick an interior row and column such that the expanded legend (anchored at marker position) fits or clips at most 1 cell, and does not collide with other expansions on the same row.
    6. Place expanded legend strings on marker rows to build the output grid.
    7. Derive the input by erasing expanded pixels, keeping only the original marker pixel and the edge legend rows.
